      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've always thought this was intended behavior, otherwise I would've reported it years ago. Figured it was to avoid blocked users from potentially harassing their blockers, or vice-versa.\n\nYou mention game worlds. Blocking situations are, overall, awkward for game worlds by nature, especially when it's a PvP game. Unfortunately the usual conclusion of it is often to just have one of the players leave (or kick them).\n\nI'm not sure if VRC is interested in \"fixing\" this (assuming it's not intended), and if it is, what the right way to go about it is.\n\nPerhaps if VRC wants, they could provide a robot avatar stand-in for blocked players in worlds that are marked as game worlds specifically (or as a feature that can be enabled/disabled in the same way that avatar scaling is). This would allow blocked players to still play in game worlds with each other and avoid it becoming a social dilemma. It may even encourage blocked players to consider unblocking and tolerating each other, discouraging insularity and toxicity on a technical level.\n\nStill doesn't fix the issue for games that require any level of talking/socializing though. It's definitely just a partial fix, where the only real fix is getting the two people to unblock each other.\n\nBut outside of that, I can honestly understand why pickups in the ownership of blocked players are also blocked. People sometimes intentionally troll/harass people who have them blocked or vice-versa with objects.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
